1
00:00:00,663 --> 00:00:02,533
(Sheldon:)Why is this so important to you?

2
00:00:02,732 --> 00:00:06,722
(Leonard:)I had enough crappy Christmases as a kid.
I'm tired of you sucking the joy out of them.

3
00:00:07,403 --> 00:00:11,433
- What was so bad about them?
- I grew up in a house full of crazy academics.

4
00:00:11,608 --> 00:00:15,808
(Leonard:)Instead of leaving Santa milk and cookies,
we had to leave him a research paper.

5
00:00:17,413 --> 00:00:21,613
(Leonard:)And in the morning, you could tell he'd been
there because the paper would be graded.

6
00:00:22,952 --> 00:00:26,552
(Sheldon:)No wonder you love Christmas.
That sounds amazing.

7
00:00:26,723 --> 00:00:31,383
(Leonard:)It wasn't amazing.
I got a C-minus four years in a row.

8
00:00:31,561 --> 00:00:34,051
(Sheldon:)I'm familiar with your work.
C-minus was your gift.

9
00:00:38,368 --> 00:00:41,808
(Raj:)Amy, I'm really sorry.
I didn't mean to upset you.

10
00:00:41,971 --> 00:00:46,131
(Amy:)It's fine. I'm used to being the girl
who never gets looked at twice.

11
00:00:46,342 --> 00:00:48,372
I didn't have my first kiss until I was 22.

12
00:00:48,544 --> 00:00:51,414
(Amy:)The guy only did it
so that I would give him back his insulin.

13
00:00:54,484 --> 00:00:59,024
(Bernadette:)Sometimes the pancreas wants
what the pancreas wants.

